Option 1 has a lower mean execution time than Option 2. The average for Option 1 is approximately 0.000938 seconds, while the average for Option 2 is approximately 0.001256 seconds. The difference between the mean execution times is:0.000318 Based on these measurements, Option 2 takes approximately 33.9% longer on average than Option 1. The standard deviation for Option 2 is also substantially larger, indicating greater variability in its recorded execution times. Welch's two-sample t-test was used to determine whether the observed difference in mean execution time is statistically significant. The test produced the following results:
